# 2. Project Objective and Build Philosophy

The current OxideOS milestone is deliberately limited.

The objective is to produce a baseline ISO that:

1. Boots successfully.
2. Loads the LXQt live desktop.
3. Provides a functioning graphical installer.
4. Completes installation onto a virtual or physical disk.
5. Boots successfully from the installed system.
6. Can be rebuilt using documented, repeatable steps.

No additional customization is permitted until this baseline has been demonstrated.

### Development principles

The project follows this sequence:

1. Make it work.
2. Understand why it works.
3. Make the build repeatable.
4. Then improve it.

This approach is intended to prevent unnecessary complexity and avoid introducing multiple variables during early development.

The project will not switch distributions or build tools without an evidenced technical reason.

