# 4. ISO Boot Architecture Investigation

## 4.1 Bootloader inspection

The original ISO was inspected using xorriso.

The ISO contains:

- BIOS GRUB boot support.
- An EFI boot image.
- MBR protective partition information.
- GPT boot information.

The ISO volume identifier is:

```text
Lubuntu 26.04.1 LTS amd64
```

The GRUB configuration was extracted to:

```text
~/OxideOS/build/grub.cfg
```

The primary boot entry is:

```text
menuentry "Try or Install Lubuntu" {
    set gfxpayload=keep
    linux  /casper/vmlinuz  --- quiet splash
    initrd /casper/initrd
}
```

Additional entries include safe graphics and OEM installation.

The primary entry does not explicitly specify a SquashFS filename or a `layerfs-path` argument.

This becomes important because the initramfs supplies a default filesystem layer independently of the GRUB configuration.

## 4.2 ISO filesystem contents

The following files were identified inside `/casper`:

| File | Approximate size |
|---|---:|
| `vmlinuz` | 16.5 MiB |
| `initrd` | 94 MiB |
| `minimal.squashfs` | 1.90 GiB |
| `minimal.standard.squashfs` | 1.58 GiB |
| `minimal.standard.live.squashfs` | 27.2 MiB |

All three SquashFS images were extracted into the build directory.

Their filesystem metadata indicates:

- SquashFS version 4.0.
- XZ compression.
- 131072-byte block size.
- Compressed metadata and data.
- Duplicate file removal enabled.

These are the three filesystem images currently known to participate in Lubuntu's live environment.

