# 6. Initramfs Investigation

The original initramfs was extracted from the ISO:

```text
/casper/initrd
```

The extracted copy is stored at:

```text
~/OxideOS/build/initrd
```

Its file size is:

```text
98,539,412 bytes
```

Initial inspection identified an SVR4 CPIO archive at the beginning of the file.

The first archive listing contained:

```text
kernel/
kernel/x86/
kernel/x86/microcode/
kernel/x86/microcode/AuthenticAMD.bin
```

The archive listing only exposed the early microcode component, not the complete initramfs.

The image was subsequently unpacked using:

```bash
unmkinitramfs ~/OxideOS/build/initrd \
  ~/OxideOS/build/initrd-inspect
```

This successfully exposed the main initramfs filesystem and its boot scripts.

The extracted inspection directory is:

```text
~/OxideOS/build/initrd-inspect/
```

This gave us access to the actual Casper scripts and configuration files.

