# 8. OverlayFS Assembly

One of the most important discoveries is how Casper combines the filesystem layers.

The extracted Casper script contains:

```bash
mount -t overlay \
  -o "upperdir=/cow/upper,lowerdir=$mounts,workdir=/cow/work" \
  "/cow" "$rootmnt" || panic "overlay mount failed"
```

This confirms that Lubuntu uses Linux OverlayFS to assemble the live environment.

### Components

| Component | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Lower directories | Provide the read-only filesystem layers |
| Upper directory | Stores writable changes |
| Work directory | Supports OverlayFS operations |
| Root mount | Receives the assembled live filesystem |

The SquashFS layers remain read-only.

The writable upper directory allows the live environment to operate as a normal working system without modifying the original SquashFS images.

This is a critical dependency for the ISO.

Any modifications to the layer names, layer files, or boot configuration must preserve the relationships expected by Casper.

