# 9. Installation Media Discovery

The following script was inspected:

```text
scripts/casper-premount/20iso_scan
```

It checks the kernel command line for:

```text
iso-scan/filename=
```

If specified, Casper searches for the ISO and records its location in:

```text
/conf/param.conf
```

The script can also record an ISO offset when the ISO is found as a file.

The normal GRUB entry does not explicitly provide this argument.

Separately, Casper's `mountroot()` function searches local devices for the live filesystem. The relevant function is:

```text
find_livefs()
```

This process checks for a specified live medium first and can subsequently scan available devices.

The boot process therefore has mechanisms for locating the live installation media rather than relying exclusively on a fixed device path.

